---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, getRelease, mb } from '../lib/site';
const rel = await getRelease();
---
<Page
  title={`Download Taskvane ${rel.version} for Windows 11 and 10 (free)`}
  h1="Download Taskvane"
  lede={`Version ${rel.version}${rel.date ? `, released ${new Date(rel.date).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}` : ''}. Free and open source, for Windows 10 (1809 or later) and Windows 11, 64-bit.`}
  description={`Download Taskvane ${rel.version}, a free Task Manager alternative for Windows 11 and 10 with CPU and GPU temperatures and power draw. Installer or portable zip, with SHA-256 checksums.`}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Download', path: '/download/' }]}
  wide
>
  <div class="choices">
    <section class="choice main">
      <h2>Installer</h2>
      <p>Recommended. Adds Taskvane to the Start menu, can set up CPU sensors for you, and can be removed from Settings &gt; Apps.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={rel.setup.url}><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg>Download installer</a>
      <p class="size num"><span class="file">{rel.setup.name}</span>{rel.setup.size ? `, ${mb(rel.setup.size)}` : ''}</p>
    </section>
    <section class="choice">
      <h2>Portable</h2>
      <p>Nothing to install. Unzip anywhere, run <code>Taskvane.exe</code>, and delete the folder when you're done. Settings stay in the folder.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href={rel.portable.url}><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg>Download portable zip</a>
      <p class="size num"><span class="file">{rel.portable.name}</span>{rel.portable.size ? `, ${mb(rel.portable.size)}` : ''}</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="prose notes">
    <h2>If Windows says "Windows protected your PC"</h2>
    <p>Taskvane isn't code-signed yet, so Microsoft SmartScreen warns about it the first time you run it. Click <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. This is common for new open-source apps, and it goes away once the app is signed.</p>
    <p>To confirm your download is the genuine file, compare its SHA-256 checksum with the one in <a href={rel.checksums}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a>:</p>
    <pre><code>Get-FileHash .\{rel.setup.name} -Algorithm SHA256</code></pre>

    <h2>Turning on CPU temperature and power</h2>
    <p>Windows only shows CPU sensors to apps running as administrator, through a signed driver called PawnIO. Taskvane doesn't bundle PawnIO; install it from its author's site, <a href="https://pawnio.eu/">pawnio.eu</a> (<strong>Enable CPU sensors</strong> in the app opens it), then restart Taskvane as administrator. <a href="/docs/#cpu-sensors">More about how this works</a>.</p>

    <h2>Code signing policy</h2>
    <p>Releases are built by GitHub Actions from the public source. We're applying for free code signing provided by SignPath.io, certificate by SignPath Foundation. Taskvane sends nothing over the network. Read the <a href="/code-signing/">code signing policy and privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Build it yourself</h2>
    <p>Prefer not to run a downloaded exe? The full source is on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a>, with build instructions in the README.</p>

    <h2>Previous versions</h2>
    <p>Every release, with notes and checksums, is on the <a href={`${SITE.repo}/releases`}>GitHub releases page</a>. See what changed in the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
  .choices { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .choice { padding: 32px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--paper); }
  .choice.main { border-color: var(--blue); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--blue); }
  .choice h2 { font-size: 34px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .choice p { color: var(--slate); max-width: 30em; }
  .choice .btn { margin-top: 8px; }
  .file { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .size { font-size: 15px; margin: 12px 0 0; }
  .notes h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .choices { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .choice { padding: 24px; } }
</style>
